{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_configuration", "label": "DevTools configuration panel (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_three_layers", "label": "The three HOCON layers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A merged tree answers what a setting is now; the question that brings you here is why it is not what you wrote, and that needs the layer as well as the value. Naming where application.conf was read from separates \"my file is being ignored\" from \"my file says something else\"."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_secret_redaction_by_key", "label": "Redaction by key, not by value", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything matching pass, secret, token, key, credential or auth is replaced before it leaves the process \u2014 by key, because a password that happens to look ordinary is still a password and the key is what names it. Blunt on purpose: a redacted tree still reveals hosts, ports, seed nodes and storage paths, so switch the panel off where that matters."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_code_options_are_not_hocon", "label": "Code options are not HOCON", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-consumer XOptions builders override HOCON at the call site and never pass through the configuration tree, so a key shown here may still be overridden by code this panel cannot see. What it shows is the HOCON resolution, exactly."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_changed_from_defaults_only", "label": "Changed-from-defaults-only filter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the filter leaves the table empty the panel says so, because nothing overriding the defaults is a worthwhile answer in itself and a different one from \"no key matches that filter\"."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_configuration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_three_layers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_configuration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_secret_redaction_by_key", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_configuration", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_changed_from_defaults_only", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/configuration.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_